# Content Creator — Tools & Skills

## Required Tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| Read | Read existing content, brand guidelines, style guides, and performance reports |
| Write | Create blog posts, social copy, email sequences, video scripts, and editorial calendars |
| WebSearch | Research topics, find data points, identify trending content, and analyze competitor content |

## Optional Tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| Edit | Refine existing content drafts, update published content, and apply editorial feedback |
| WebFetch | Pull specific web pages for research, reference data, and competitor analysis |

## Recommended Skills

### seo-optimize
Analyze content for SEO completeness — keyword density, meta tags, header structure, internal linking, and featured snippet formatting.

### tone-check
Validate content against the brand voice guidelines ({{brand_voice}}). Flag deviations and suggest revisions that maintain consistency.

## Tool Configuration Notes

- **Research depth**: For long-form content, conduct at least 3 searches to triangulate facts and gather diverse perspectives.
- **Image direction**: When creating blog posts or social content, include visual direction notes (suggested images, infographic data, chart descriptions) even though image generation isn't available.
- **Link strategy**: Include internal link suggestions pointing to related content within the existing content library.
- **Headline testing**: For every piece, generate 3-5 headline variations optimized for different platforms and audience segments.

